# CCH standing rules

These were previously Cursor **User Rules**, which live in Cursor's settings and are wiped
by a reset. Moved into the repo Aug 30, 2026 so they survive one. Nothing to paste.

## Workspace

- Canonical repo: `C:\dev\CCH-Platform-Deploy\cch-deploy` **only**.
- Never read or write `C:\Users\cindy\Dropbox\CCH-Platform-Deploy\`.

## Work orders — every change gets a number

A code change is a work order, whether it came from the queue or from a chat message.

- Before the first edit: read `loop/LOOP_LEDGER.md`, take the next number, add an
  `IN PROGRESS` row, and say the number in chat.
- On finish, all three steps: `loop/WO-###_DONE_CR_[MonDD].md`; a `_DEPLOY_QUEUE.md` line
  **with the WO number after the date stamp**; the ledger row set to `DONE-UNVERIFIED`.
- Never set `VERIFIED` yourself. No size floor. No "too small for a WO."

Detail: `wo-number-every-change.mdc`.

## Staging is the default; print is not waivable

- Staging (`cch-platform-staging.web.app`) and production (`cch-platform.web.app`) are
  **different Firebase projects**. No shared data. A prod doc may not exist on staging;
  that is expected, not a bug.
- The chat that builds a feature deploys it to **staging** and keeps fixing there. Canon: `loop/CCH_STUDIO_DEPLOY_RULE_CW_Oct16.md` (Cindy Oct 16, 2026).
- Production hosting needs Cindy's explicit typed **GO**, every time. Only Cursor #1 deploys production.
- Before a production deploy, check what is already live so nothing newer gets overwritten.
- Anything paid, ordered, or approved is locked.
- Changes to the print/PDF layer (`@media print`, `@page`, Bill To / Ship To, the line-item
  block) go to **staging only** and do **not** take a same-session production GO.

## Print is shared by four documents

Proposals, invoices, POs, tear sheets. Verify a print change against **all four**, not
against the one that prompted it. Verifying 9.9.278 on a proposal alone is how PO print
broke. Never restyle Bill To / Ship To / line items to make one document "match" another
unless Cindy asked for that specific change.

Detail: `print-surface-lock.mdc`.

## Code grounding — mandatory, no guessing

Before any claim about code behavior, root cause, or any code edit: grep 3+ aliases, read
the function body **this turn**, cite `file:line`. Memory, session logs, and handoff notes
are **not** evidence. If unsure, say what you searched. On **RELOOK** or **GROUNDING CHECK**:
stop recommending, show grep results.

Canon: `CODE_GROUNDING_PROTOCOL_MH_May13_v1.0.md` in repo root.

## Asymmetric gates get reported, not silently half-fixed

When a gate names some document types and not others (for example
`type === 'proposal' || type === 'invoice'` with POs excluded), that asymmetry is usually
the real bug rather than the thing you were sent to fix. Say so before editing.

## Secrets

Never paste API keys, PATs, or secrets in chat. Use local `*-pat.env` files and
`firebase secrets:set`.

## Studio vocabulary

"Preview" often means the client PDF popup. Client invoice UX belongs on the **main invoice
page** (Client View / Manage / Print), not only in Preview.

## Deploys

Explain deploy steps in plain PowerShell, one command per step. No `curl` for secrets.
